# Environments. Each is a pinned stack for exactly ONE dependency set, rebuilt
# by scripts/, never committed. They must not reference each other: openpi pins
# jax 0.5.3 + torch 2.7.1 + numpy<2, the LIBERO venv pins robosuite 1.4.1 +
# mujoco 3.1.6, and the only thing installed in both is the pure-python
# openpi-client.
.venv/
.venv-*/

# Upstream checkouts and their checkpoints. Reproduced by:
#   scripts/setup_libero.sh   robosuite/mujoco/numpy pins + LIBERO checkout
#   scripts/serve_pi05.sh     openpi (expects `uv sync` in third_party/openpi)
# Tens of GB of model weights; nothing here belongs in git.
third_party/
!third_party/LIBERO.commit

# THE SCRIPTS THAT REBUILD THE ABOVE ARE TRACKED, DELIBERATELY.
# A previous `scripts/` was never committed. When the working tree was cleared,
# third_party/ and five venvs went with it and the recipe to rebuild them did
# not exist anywhere. Ignoring the outputs is correct; ignoring the recipe is
# how a project becomes unreproducible in one command.
!scripts/

# Generated training datasets (overlay-augmented RoboCasa replays).
# Rebuilt by examples/emit_lerobot.py; tens of GB of video.
data/

# Fine-tuning outputs. ~22 GB per checkpoint (weights + optimizer state), and
# reproducible from scripts/finetune_overlay.sh + examples/emit_lerobot.py.
# The whole directory, not just the weights: extension globs let the fragments
# through (config.json, trainer_state.json, training_args.bin, and rng_state
# is .pth not .pt), and a checkpoint without its weights is not a checkpoint.
checkpoints/

# damped-plan records ARE committed -- plans, evidence and the append-only
# events.jsonl are plain JSON that diffs well, and this project's value is
# disproportionately in its retracted claims. Only the runtime lock is not.
.damped-plan/.lock

# Model caches
.cache/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.ckpt

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Rollout traces and scratch outputs
results/
*.jsonl
# ...but NOT damped-plan's append-only event log, which the *.jsonl rule
# above would otherwise swallow. It is the audit trail of every state
# transition and is the whole point of committing .damped-plan/.
!.damped-plan/events.jsonl

# textbook-index MCP: the concept graph and hybrid index are derived from the
# PDFs in docs/ and are rebuilt on first tool call.
kuzu_concept_db*

# component-belief MCP: the evidence ledger IS committed on purpose; the
# derived belief cache is regenerable from evidence + declarations.
.belief/cache/

# Frozen-feature cache: 168 MB derived from the demonstrations by
# tools/cache_features.py, and regenerable by rerunning it.
cache/
runs/

# The textbook is a copyrighted third-party document, not project source. It is
# read through the textbook-index MCP from a local path; docs/*.md reference it
# by section rather than reproducing it.
docs/*.pdf
